From 76fa3b7477bbb31210997f6601b54bfb2ffc319f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 04:11:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/17] docs: document metrics, trace context and logging

Operators need to know what the two /metrics endpoints expose and how
they are protected before pointing Prometheus at them, and how to
follow one request through the gateway and control plane logs.

The root README gains an observability section: the control plane
metrics, the protection decision (no authentication, aggregate data
only, bounded labels, keep both endpoints off public ingress), the
trace context rules and the log format, plus FORGEMESH_LOG_FORMAT and
FORGEMESH_LOG_LEVEL in the configuration table. The gateway README
documents its metrics, route classes, access log, trace headers and
the new middleware order, and moves probes and /metrics out of the
authenticated path in the request diagram, which is where the router
mounts them. CHANGELOG and module-mapping list the new modules, hooks
and tests, with the file counts of this branch.

The outbox documentation said that under forgemesh-control-plane the
default publisher writes events to stdout. Now that the entry point
configures logging, events go through the same handler as every other
log record, on stderr and at a fixed INFO level, so the README events
paragraph and the dispatcher's CHANGELOG entry say so. The REST API
section lists traceId in the error envelope, and the lock wait metric
is described as covering the whole database, since the registry, the
outbox and the audit log share one connection and lock.
